traceability.evidence:
Key implementation and tests:

1) Story presence and direct linkage
- Story file exists: docs/stories/010.1-DEV-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS.story.md
- tests/rules/valid-annotation-format.test.ts header:
  * Tests for: docs/stories/010.1-DEV-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS.story.md
  * @story docs/stories/010.1-DEV-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS.story.md
  * @req REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-STORY
  * @req REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-REQ
  * @req REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-EXAMPLES
  * @req REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-FALLBACK
- Jest run (npm test -- --runInBand --verbose) shows this suite passing under "Valid Annotation Format Rule (Story 005.0-DEV-ANNOTATION-VALIDATION)", with all REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-* tests passing.

2) Core Functionality & Pattern config (REQ-PATTERN-CONFIG; Core Functionality AC)
- src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-options.ts:
  ```ts
  export interface AnnotationRuleOptions {
    story?: { pattern?: string; example?: string };
    req?: { pattern?: string; example?: string };
    storyPathPattern?: string;
    storyPathExample?: string;
    requirementIdPattern?: string;
    requirementIdExample?: string;
  }
  ```
- resolveOptions reads both nested and flat options and resolves them into runtime patterns/examples:
  ```ts
  const nestedStoryPattern = user?.story?.pattern;
  const flatStoryPattern = user?.storyPathPattern;
  const nestedReqPattern = user?.req?.pattern;
  const flatReqPattern = user?.requirementIdPattern;
  ...
  const storyPattern = resolvePattern({ nestedPattern: nestedStoryPattern, nestedFieldName: "story.pattern", flatPattern: flatStoryPattern, flatFieldName: "storyPathPattern", defaultPattern: getDefaultStoryPattern() });
  const reqPattern = resolvePattern({ nestedPattern: nestedReqPattern, nestedFieldName: "req.pattern", flatPattern: flatReqPattern, flatFieldName: "requirementIdPattern", defaultPattern: getDefaultReqPattern() });
  ```
- Tests in tests/rules/valid-annotation-format.test.ts (all passing):
  - Nested pattern config examples:
    ```ts
    { name: "[REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-STORY] custom storyPathPattern accepts alternate extension",
      code: `// @story stories/feature-010.1-CUSTOM.story.mdx`,
      options: [{ story: { pattern: "^stories\\/[^\\s]+\\.story\\.mdx$", example: "stories/example-010.1-CUSTOM.story.mdx" } }], },
    { name: "[REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-REQ] custom requirementIdPattern accepts PROJECT-123 style IDs",
      code: `// @req PROJECT-123`,
      options: [{ req: { pattern: "^[A-Z]+-[0-9]+$", example: "PROJECT-123" } }], },
    ```
  - Flat shorthand examples:
    ```ts
    { name: "[REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-STORY-FLAT] flat storyPathPattern accepts alternate extension when nested config not provided",
      code: `// @story stories/feature-010.1-CUSTOM.story.mdx`,
      options: [{ storyPathPattern: "^stories\\/[^\\s]+\\.story\\.mdx$", storyPathExample: "stories/example-010.1-CUSTOM.story.mdx" }], },
    { name: "[REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-REQ-FLAT] flat requirementIdPattern accepts PROJECT-123 style IDs when nested config not provided",
      code: `// @req PROJECT-123`,
      options: [{ requirementIdPattern: "^[A-Z]+-[0-9]+$", requirementIdExample: "PROJECT-123" }], },
    ```

3) Backward compatibility and defaults (REQ-BACKWARD-COMPAT; Backward Compatibility AC)
- Default patterns/examples (valid-annotation-options.ts):
  ```ts
  function getDefaultStoryPattern(): RegExp { return /^docs\/stories\/[0-9]+\.[0-9]+-DEV-[\w-]+\.story\.md$/; }
  function getDefaultStoryExample(): string { return "docs/stories/005.0-DEV-EXAMPLE.story.md"; }
  function getDefaultReqPattern(): RegExp { return /^REQ-[A-Z0-9-]+$/; }
  export function getDefaultReqExample(): string { return "REQ-EXAMPLE"; }
  ```
- resolvePattern falls back when no options given:
  ```ts
  if (!effective) { return defaultPattern; }
  ```
- resolveExample falls back when no examples given:
  ```ts
  return defaultExample;
  ```
- Tests confirm that invalid custom patterns fall back to default behavior while still reporting configuration errors:
  ```ts
  { name: "[REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-FALLBACK] invalid storyPathPattern falls back to default behavior",
    code: `// @story docs/stories/005.0-DEV-ANNOTATION-VALIDATION.story`,
    options: [{ story: { pattern: "[unclosed" } }],
    output: `// @story docs/stories/005.0-DEV-ANNOTATION-VALIDATION.story.md`,
    errors: [
      { messageId: "invalidRuleConfiguration", data: { details: 'Invalid regular expression for option "story.pattern": "[unclosed"' } },
      { messageId: "invalidStoryFormat", ... },
    ], },
  { name: "[REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-FALLBACK-FLAT] invalid flat storyPathPattern falls back to default and reports config error",
    options: [{ storyPathPattern: "[unclosed" }],
    output: `// @story ... .story.md`,
    errors: [ { messageId: "invalidRuleConfiguration", ... }, { messageId: "invalidStoryFormat", ... } ], },
  ```

4) Pattern validation and configuration errors (REQ-REGEX-VALIDATION; Pattern Validation AC)
- Regex validation in resolvePattern (valid-annotation-options.ts):
  ```ts
  let optionErrors: string[] = [];
  function buildInvalidRegexError(field: string, pattern: string): string {
    return `Invalid regular expression for option "${field}": "${pattern}"`;
  }
  function resolvePattern(...) {
    ...
    try {
      return new RegExp(effective.value);
    } catch {
      optionErrors.push(buildInvalidRegexError(effective.field, effective.value));
      return defaultPattern;
    }
  }
  ```
- Rule reads and reports optionErrors in src/rules/valid-annotation-format.ts:
  ```ts
  meta: {
    messages: {
      invalidRuleConfiguration:
        "Invalid configuration for valid-annotation-format: {{details}}",
    },
    schema: getRuleSchema(),
    ...
  },
  create(context: any) {
    const options = resolveOptions(context.options || []);
    const optionErrors = getOptionErrors();
    return {
      Program(node: any) {
        if (optionErrors && optionErrors.length > 0) {
          optionErrors.forEach((details: string) => {
            context.report({ node, messageId: "invalidRuleConfiguration", data: { details } });
          });
        }
        ...
      },
    };
  },
  ```
- Tests cover invalid nested and flat regex options for both story and req patterns (all passing):
  - invalid story.pattern / req.pattern
  - invalid storyPathPattern / requirementIdPattern
  Each expects an invalidRuleConfiguration diagnostic with the exact error text.

5) Error messages and examples (REQ-EXAMPLE-MESSAGES; Error Messages AC)
- Example resolution (valid-annotation-options.ts): nested overrides flat and both override defaults:
  ```ts
  const storyExample = resolveExample(nestedStoryExample, flatStoryExample, getDefaultStoryExample());
  const reqExample = resolveExample(nestedReqExample, flatReqExample, getDefaultReqExample());
  ```
- Error message builders use options.storyExample and options.reqExample (valid-annotation-utils.ts):
  ```ts
  export function buildStoryErrorMessage(kind, value, options) {
    const example = options.storyExample || STORY_EXAMPLE_PATH;
    ...
  }
  export function buildReqErrorMessage(kind, value, options) {
    const example = options.reqExample || getDefaultReqExample();
    ...
  }
  ```
- Tests verifying custom and override behavior:
  ```ts
  { name: "[REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-EXAMPLES] custom story example appears in error message",
    options: [{ story: { pattern: "^stories...", example: "stories/example-010.1-CUSTOM.story.mdx" } }],
    errors[0].data.details includes that custom example,
  },
  { name: "[REQ-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS-EXAMPLES] custom requirement example appears in error message",
    options: [{ req: { pattern: "^[A-Z]+-[0-9]+$", example: "PROJECT-123" } }],
    errors[0].data.details uses "PROJECT-123",
  },
  { name: "[REQ-EXAMPLE-MESSAGES] nested story example text overrides flat storyPathExample in error messages",
    options: [{ story: { example: "stories/special/example.story.mdx" }, storyPathExample: "stories/ignored/example.story.mdx" }],
    error details use the nested example,
  },
  { name: "[REQ-EXAMPLE-MESSAGES] nested req example text overrides flat requirementIdExample in error messages",
    options: [{ req: { example: "REQ-FOO-001" }, requirementIdExample: "PROJECT-123" }],
    error details use "REQ-FOO-001",
  },
  ```

6) Schema / quality standards (REQ-SCHEMA-VALIDATION; Quality Standards AC)
- JSON Schema definition for rule options (valid-annotation-options.ts):
  ```ts
  export function getRuleSchema() {
    return [
      {
        type: "object",
        properties: {
          story: {
            type: "object",
            properties: { pattern: { type: "string" }, example: { type: "string" } },
            additionalProperties: false,
          },
          req: {
            type: "object",
            properties: { pattern: { type: "string" }, example: { type: "string" } },
            additionalProperties: false,
          },
          storyPathPattern: { type: "string" },
          storyPathExample: { type: "string" },
          requirementIdPattern: { type: "string" },
          requirementIdExample: { type: "string" },
        },
        additionalProperties: false,
      },
    ];
  }
  ```
- Rule meta hooks this schema into ESLint: `schema: getRuleSchema()`.

7) Integration with valid-story-reference and configuration consistency (REQ-CONSISTENCY; Integration AC)
- valid-story-reference (src/rules/valid-story-reference.ts) uses:
  ```ts
  const defaultStoryDirs = ["docs/stories", "stories"];
  ```
  and options `storyDirectories`, `allowAbsolutePaths`, `requireStoryExtension` (verified by tests/config/eslint-config-validation.test.ts).
- valid-annotation-format’s default story pattern `^docs/stories/[0-9]+\.[0-9]+-DEV-[\w-]+\.story\.md$` is consistent with the default docs/stories directory used by valid-story-reference, and the pattern options are purely syntactic checks (no filesystem access). All tests for both rules pass together, showing the new pattern configuration does not break storyDirectories-based behavior.

8) Documentation of custom pattern configuration (Documentation AC)
- user-docs/api-reference.md, section "traceability/valid-annotation-format":
  - Describes nested config:
    - `story.pattern` / `story.example`
    - `req.pattern` / `req.example`
  - Explicitly documents flat shorthands:
    ```md
    For backward compatibility, the rule also supports flat shorthand fields:
    - storyPathPattern – Shorthand for story.pattern ...
    - storyPathExample – Shorthand for story.example ...
    - requirementIdPattern – Shorthand for req.pattern ...
    - requirementIdExample – Shorthand for req.example ...
    ```
  - Notes behavior: patterns are optional, invalid patterns cause configuration errors, and omitting options preserves original behavior.
- Combined with the tested configuration examples in tests/rules/valid-annotation-format.test.ts (matching the story’s use cases), this satisfies the requirement for clear documentation of custom pattern configuration.

All of the above behavior is validated by a passing Jest run on the full suite, including all tests tagged for story 010.1-DEV-CONFIGURABLE-PATTERNS.
